Subject: server: no static address-to-integer initializer for VSI C

server_main_loop() initialises a static pointer with
(connection *)(uintptr_t)&log_con_jqueue.  VSI C rejects converting an
address through an integer in a static initializer (%CC-E-BADSTATICCVT);
upstream already drops 'static' here for MSVC.  Do the same on VMS: the
value is a constant address either way.

--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -2263,7 +2263,7 @@
 			server_load_check(srv);
 		}
 
-	  #ifndef _MSC_VER
+	  #if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(__VMS)
 		static
 	  #endif
 		connection * const sentinel =
